# React 19 form event types

This repo uses `react@19` with `@types/react@19.2+`: `React.FormEvent` and `React.FormEventHandler` are deprecated. Use `React.SubmitEvent` / `React.SubmitEventHandler` for form submits.

```tsx
// Deprecated.
const onSubmit: React.FormEventHandler<HTMLFormElement> = (e) => { /* ... */ };

// Avoid splitting preventDefault from submit logic.
<form onSubmit={(event) => { event.preventDefault(); void handleSubmit(); }}>

// Preferred.
async function onSubmit(event: React.SubmitEvent<HTMLFormElement>) {
  event.preventDefault();
}

<form onSubmit={onSubmit}>
```

- Prefer a named submit handler when it keeps `preventDefault` and submit logic together.
- Use `useActionState` + `<form action={...}>` for server work.
- Plain typed `onSubmit` is still appropriate for client SDK flows such as `authClient.*`.
